Fri Nov 27 05:51:13 UTC 2026 - Johannes Kastl <opensuse_buildservice@ojkastl.de>

- Update to version 0.7.9:
  ktop v0.7.9 introduces the [4] Storage and [5] Network TUI tabs,
  live kubelet volume capacity and inode utilization telemetry,
  EndpointSlice readiness health tracking, cAdvisor network packet
  drop and error rates, matching --noui snapshot schema additions,
  and Pod Detail storage/network enrichments (#178).
  * Storage Telemetry & [4] Storage Tab (prom, metrics,
    views/model, k8s, views/storage)
    - Kubelet Volume Metrics Scraping (prom/types.go,
      metrics/source.go, metrics/prom/prom_source.go): Added
      kubelet_volume_stats_{capacity_bytes,used_bytes,available_bytes,inodes,inodes_used}
      to DefaultMetricAllowlist and implemented
      metrics.VolumeStatsProvider
      (PromMetricsSource.GetAllVolumeStats) to aggregate per-PVC
      byte usage, fill percentage, and inode utilization
      percentages.
    - Storage View Models & Controller
      (views/model/storage_model.go, k8s/client_controller.go,
      k8s/storage_controller.go): Added normalized PVCModel,
      PVModel, StorageClassModel, StorageSummary, and
      StorageSnapshot types alongside sorting helpers
      (SortPVCModelsBy, SortPVModelsBy). Added startup RBAC
      capability checks for StorageClass alongside existing
      PersistentVolume and PersistentVolumeClaim informers,
      exposing Controller.GetStorageSnapshot and
      SetStorageRefreshFunc.
    - [4] Storage TUI Page (views/storage/summary.go,
      views/storage/page.go): Added a 1-line summary bar displaying
      bound/pending PVCs, >=85% fill alert count, PV bound totals,
      StorageClasses, used/capacity totals, and disk read/write
      rates, paired with interactive sortable/filterable
      PersistentVolumeClaims (FILL% and INODES% highlighted at
      >=85% warning and >=95% error thresholds) and
      PersistentVolumes tables, y clipboard copy, / row filtering,
      global namespace filter sync, and Enter YAML inspection
      modals.
  * Network Telemetry & [5] Network Tab (prom, metrics,
    views/model, k8s, views/network)
    - cAdvisor Drop & Error Counters (prom/types.go,
      prom/scraper.go, metrics/source.go,
      metrics/prom/prom_source.go): Added
      container_network_{receive,transmit}_{packets_dropped,errors}_total
      to DefaultMetricAllowlist and updated
      shouldKeepCAdvisorSeries to retain both node-root (id="/")
      and pod-sandbox (container="POD") series for drop and error
      counters. Implemented metrics.NetworkErrorsProvider
      (GetClusterNetworkErrorRates and GetPodNetworkErrorRates).
    - Network View Models & Controller
      (views/model/network_model.go, k8s/client_controller.go,
      k8s/network_controller.go): Added normalized ServiceModel
      (with HasEndpointAlert()), IngressModel, NodeNetworkModel,
      NetworkSummary, and NetworkSnapshot types with
      SortServiceModelsBy and SortIngressModelsBy. Added RBAC-gated
      informers for Service, EndpointSlice (discovery.k8s.io/v1),
      and Ingress with deduplicated ready/total endpoint
      aggregation in Controller.GetNetworkSnapshot.
    - [5] Network TUI Page (views/network/summary.go,
      views/network/page.go): Added a summary strip reporting total
      Services, zero-endpoint alert counts, Ingresses, cluster
      RX/TX throughput, and drop/error rates, paired with Services
      (highlighting selector-backed services with zero ready
      endpoints) and Ingresses tables, / row filtering, y copy, and
      Enter YAML modals.
  * Snapshots, Pod Detail, Navigation & Documentation
    (internal/snapshot, collector, views/overview, views/pod,
    application, config, cmd, ui, docs, hack/load-test)
    - Headless Snapshot & Collector Support
      (internal/snapshot/snapshot.go, internal/snapshot/builder.go,
      collector/collector.go, collector/k8s_provider.go): Extended
      Snapshot, BuildInput, and collector.Aggregate with Storage
      (*StorageData) and Network (*NetworkData) sections, added
      VolumeUsages, NetworkDropsPerSec, and NetworkErrorsPerSec on
      PodData, and updated Snapshot.Clone() to deep-copy all nested
      slices.
    - Pod Detail Enrichments (views/overview/main_panel.go,
      views/pod/detail.go): Joined mounted PVC usage stats and
      per-pod network drop/error rates in buildPodDetailData,
      rendering PVCs: fill percentages (colored at >=85% and >=95%)
      and non-zero NetErr: counters inside the Pod Detail view.
    - Navigation, CLI, Docs & Load Test Fixtures (application/,
      config/, cmd/, ui/, docs/, hack/load-test/): Registered [4]
      Storage (PageStorage) and [5] Network (PageNetwork), added
      storage and network to --page / ui.default_page validation
      and ui.StorageContext / ui.NetworkContext footers, updated
      docs/cli.md, docs/noui.md, and docs/prometheus.md, and
      expanded hack/load-test/ with live PVC/PV disk I/O and
      Service/Ingress/HTTP traffic workloads.
  * Upgrade & Compatibility Notes
    - Backward Compatibility: Fully compatible with existing CLI
      flags, kubectl ktop plugin invocation, ~/.ktop/config.yaml,
      and existing --noui JSON/JSONL consumers; new storage,
      network, and per-pod fields are additive with omitempty.
    - RBAC Resilience: StorageClass, Service, EndpointSlice, and
      Ingress informers probe cluster permissions on startup and
      degrade without error if RBAC restricts listing optional
      resources.
    - Deprecations & Migration Actions: None.

