Thu Nov 26 06:35:56 UTC 2026 - Johannes Kastl <opensuse_buildservice@ojkastl.de>

- Update to version 0.7.8:
  ktop v0.7.8 resolves unbounded memory growth and scrape-time heap
  spikes in the built-in Prometheus metrics collector (#176), fixes
  ~/.ktop/config.yaml Prometheus configuration loading, and updates
  Prometheus and CLI memory-tuning documentation.
  * Prometheus Store & Ring Buffer Memory Fixes (prom)
    - Lazy Ring Buffer Allocation (prom/ring_buffer.go): RingBuffer
      now allocates backing storage lazily starting at 16 slots and
      doubles up to its configured capacity rather than
      pre-allocating MaxSamples (10,000 × 24 bytes = 240 KB)
      immediately per series. Clear() zeroes backing elements to
      avoid retaining references.
      - Retention-Bounded Per-Series Capacity (prom/storage.go):
        InMemoryStore bounds effective per-series ring buffer
        capacity to what RetentionTime / ScrapeInterval (+
        headroom) can produce, clamped to MaxSamples, preventing
        long-running active series from growing to 10,000 slots
        over extended uptime.
      - Metadata & Stale Series Reclamation (prom/storage.go,
        prom/controller.go):
        - Removed the unbounded stringHandles map and delegated
          InternString directly to unique.Make(s).Value() so
          interned strings for deleted pods, containers, and cgroup
          paths are eligible for garbage collection.
        - Rebuilt labelNames and labelValues and compacted heavily
          shrunk per-metric series maps during
          cleanupExpiredSamples.
        - Capped the periodic cleanup interval to at most 2 minutes
          so expired series are reclaimed promptly.
      - Reduced Query Allocations (prom/storage.go): Added
        QueryLatestPerSeries for single-sample lookups and
        batch-allocated MetricSample slices in QueryRangePerSeries.
  * Streaming Scrape Filtering & cAdvisor Cardinality Reduction
    (prom/scraper.go)
    - Stream-Filtered Parsing: scrapeTarget streams responses via
      req.Stream and filters Prometheus exposition lines against
      DefaultMetricAllowlist before invoking expfmt.TextParser,
      avoiding protobuf DTO allocation for non-allowlisted metric
      families.
    - Bounded Node Concurrency: scrapeAllTargets caps concurrent
      node scrapes at 6 to bound peak heap usage on multi-node
      clusters.
    - cAdvisor Series Filtering: Drops unqueried cAdvisor series
      during ingestion—including non-root/non-pod systemd and slice
      cgroups (/system.slice/*, /kubepods.slice), pause containers
      (container="POD"), per-core pod CPU series, pod-level network
      series, and non-workload CFS/PSI series—while preserving all
      queried node (id="/", including cgroups v1 per-core CPU
      fallback) and pod/container series (including static-pod
      container="" memory fallback).
  * Refresh Allocation & Config Wiring Fixes (metrics/prom, k8s,
    views/node, cmd, docs)
    - Latest-Sample Memory Lookups (metrics/prom/prom_source.go):
      GetAllPodMetrics and queryLatestSumFiltered use
      QueryLatestPerSeries for working-set memory instead of
      scanning 5-minute ranges on every 3-second pod refresh.
    - Informer Read Without Deep Copy (k8s/pods_controller.go):
      GetPodModels reads node allocatable resources directly from
      the node informer lister without deep-copying full Node
      objects.
    - Reusable Node Info Header (views/node/detail.go): Reuses a
      single tview.TextView in drawInfoHeader across refreshes.
    - Config File Prometheus Settings (cmd/ktop.go): Applied
      metrics.scrape_interval, metrics.retention,
      metrics.max_samples, and metrics.components from
      ~/.ktop/config.yaml when not overridden by CLI flags.
    - Documentation (docs/prometheus.md, docs/cli.md): Updated
      default --prometheus-scrape-interval documentation to 5s and
      added a Memory Tuning guide covering CLI flags,
      ~/.ktop/config.yaml, --ksm=off,
      --metrics-source=metrics-server, and GOMEMLIMIT.
  * Upgrade & Compatibility Notes
    - Backward Compatibility: Fully backward compatible with
      existing CLI flags, kubectl ktop plugin usage,
      ~/.ktop/config.yaml files, and --noui JSON/JSONL output.
    - Deprecations & Retractions: None.
    - Migration Actions: None required. Existing
      ~/.ktop/config.yaml files with max_samples: 10000 benefit
      automatically from lazy ring-buffer allocation and
      retention-bounded per-series caps.

