Tue Nov 24 10:05:14 UTC 2026 - Johannes Kastl <opensuse_buildservice@ojkastl.de>

- Update to version 0.7.7:
  ktop v0.7.6 introduces a dedicated [3] Events tab for live,
  cluster- and namespace-wide Kubernetes Event monitoring, adds a
  floating Event Detail modal with full untruncated messages and
  cross-tab object inspection, exposes normalized events in --noui
  JSON/JSONL snapshots, and refines top-level tab navigation with <
  / > shortcuts.
  Operators can switch directly to [3] Events (via key 3, < / >,
  --page=events, or ui.default_page: events), filter down to
  Warnings (w), pause live updates during event storms (f) while
  tracking incoming event deltas, open any event in a floating
  modal to read full word-wrapped messages, inspect raw Event YAML
  (v), or jump directly to the involved Pod, Node, Deployment,
  StatefulSet, DaemonSet, or Job (g).
  * Standalone [3] Events Page & Floating Event Detail Modal
    (views/events, application, ui, config, cmd)
    - Cluster-Wide Chronological Event Stream
      - Problem / Context: Events were previously visible only
        inside single-object detail views (Node Detail, Pod Detail,
        and Workload Detail), providing no cluster- or
        namespace-wide feed for cross-resource warnings such as
        scheduling failures, image pull errors, mount failures, or
        eviction cascades.
      - Technical Implementation: Added the views/events package
        (views/events/page.go, views/events/summary.go,
        views/events/detail_modal.go) and registered [3] Events
        (application.PageEvents) in application/tui/app.go. Added
        "events" to config.ValidPages (config/config.go) and
        updated --page in cmd/ktop.go. Added ui.EventsContext and
        ui.EventDetailModalContext in ui/footer_context.go.
      - Behavioral Notes:
        - Single-line Summary bar displays Events, Warnings,
          Normal, top firing Reason (prioritizing Warning reasons
          when present), and active stream badges (ALL | WARNINGS
          ONLY, LIVE | PAUSED (+N new)).
        - Table columns: LAST SEEN | TYPE | REASON | OBJECT | NS |
          COUNT | MESSAGE using ui.TableController for column
          sorting, / substring filtering, and y clipboard copy.
        - Key w toggles Warnings-only filtering; key f
          freezes/resumes live table updates while tracking new
          event arrivals in the summary bar. Both keys are
          suppressed while editing / filter input.
        - Syncs automatically with the global namespace filter
          shared across Overview and Workloads.
    - Floating Event Detail Modal & Cross-Tab Object Jump
      - Problem / Context: Single-line event table rows truncate
        long Kubernetes event messages and require manual
        navigation to inspect the affected workload, pod, or node.
      - Technical Implementation: Implemented events.DetailModal
        (views/events/detail_modal.go) on ui.OverlayFrame, showing
        normalized metadata (Type, Reason, Object, Count, First
        Seen, Last Seen, Source, Event Name) above a scrollable,
        word-wrapped full message view. Added
        Application.JumpToObject(kind, namespace, name) and
        application.IsInspectableObjectKind(kind) in
        application/app_ctrl.go.
      - Behavioral Notes:
        - Pressing Enter on an event opens the floating Event
          Detail modal (ESC / q closes and restores table focus; y
          copies the full message; v opens raw Event YAML via
          k8s.FormatObjectYAML).
        - Pressing g jumps to the involved resource when
          inspectable: Pod opens the shared floating Pod Inspector
          modal over [3] Events, Node switches to [1] Overview and
          opens Node Detail, and
          Deployment/StatefulSet/DaemonSet/Job switches to [2]
          Workloads and opens Workload Detail. Missing or
          already-deleted objects display a warning toast instead
          of opening an empty view.
  * Normalized Event Model, Informer Controller & --noui Snapshot
    (views/model, k8s, internal/snapshot, collector)
    - Unified core/v1 and events.k8s.io/v1 Event Normalization
      - Problem / Context: Controllers emitting events.k8s.io/v1
        events populate Series.LastObservedTime, Series.Count,
        EventTime, and ReportingController rather than legacy
        LastTimestamp, Count, and Source.Component, causing
        incomplete counts or misordered timelines.
      - Technical Implementation: Added views/model/event_model.go
        (EventModel, EventsSummary, EventsSnapshot, NewEventModel,
        EventLastTimestamp, EventFirstTimestamp, EventCount,
        EventSource, ComputeEventsSummary, SortEventModelsBy).
        Added k8s/events_controller.go (SetEventsRefreshFunc,
        GetEventsSnapshot, HasObject) backed by the existing shared
        coreInformers.Events() informer with no additional API
        watch or RBAC requirement. Updated sortEventsByTime in
        k8s/client_funcs.go to use model.EventLastTimestamp.
      - APIs / Signatures:

        snap, err := ctrl.GetEventsSnapshot(ctx, k8s.AllNamespaces, k8s.DefaultTUIEventsLimit)
        exists := ctrl.HasObject("Pod", "default", "api-0")

    - events Field in internal/snapshot and Headless --noui Output
      - Problem / Context: Headless --noui JSON/JSONL reports
        previously omitted cluster event summaries and recent event
        records.
      - Technical Implementation: Added EventsData,
        EventsSummaryData, and EventData (json:"events,omitempty")
        to snapshot.Snapshot with deep-copy support in
        Snapshot.Clone() (internal/snapshot/snapshot.go) and
        conversion helpers (eventsDataFromModel, ToEventsSnapshot)
        in internal/snapshot/builder.go. Populated
        BuildInput.Events in collector/k8s_provider.go (bounded by
        k8s.DefaultSnapshotEventsLimit) and propagated Events onto
        collector.Aggregate (collector/collector.go).
      - APIs / Signatures:

        {
          "events": {
            "summary": {
              "total": 12,
              "warning_count": 2,
              "normal_count": 10,
              "top_reason": "BackOff",
              "top_reason_count": 2
            },
            "items": []
          }
        }

  * Tab Navigation & Help Overlay Refinement (application, ui, docs)
    - < / > Page Navigation & Clearer Help Labels
      - Problem / Context: Square-bracket page navigation ([ / ])
        rendered ambiguously in the keyboard shortcuts help overlay
        (1-3 / [ / ]).
      - Technical Implementation: Replaced [ / ] global
        page-switching bindings with < (PrevPage) and > (NextPage)
        in application/app_ctrl.go. Updated ui/help_modal.go to
        display separate Keys 1-3 and < or > lines, escaped key
        labels via tview.Escape, and updated docs/guide.md,
        docs/cli.md, and docs/noui.md.
  * Upgrade & Compatibility Notes
    - Backward Compatibility: Fully backward compatible with
      existing ktop CLI flags, kubectl ktop plugin usage,
      ~/.ktop/config.yaml configurations, and --noui JSON/JSONL
      consumers (events is an additive omitempty field).
    - Behavioral Changes: Sequential previous/next tab navigation
      now uses < and > (Shift+, / Shift+.) instead of [ and ].
      Direct numeric tab switching (1–3) is unchanged.
    - Migration Actions: None required.
- Update to version 0.7.6:
  ktop v0.7.7 adds auto-discovered kube-state-metrics (KSM)
  governance telemetry, built-in Kubernetes Component SLIs
  (/metrics/slis) and Kubelet probe counters (/metrics/probes),
  lock-free joins into both the interactive TUI and headless --noui
  JSON/JSONL snapshots, and an always-visible Overview Cluster
  Summary layout for terminals of 45 rows or fewer.
  Operators gain live visibility into control-plane and kubelet
  healthcheck SLIs (incorporated into cluster health_score when
  explicitly unhealthy), failing readiness/liveness/startup probes,
  HPA scaling ceilings, PDB disruption budgets, ResourceQuota
  utilization, CronJob schedules, pod disruption reasons, and DRA
  ResourceClaim associations—with silent degradation when KSM or
  SLI endpoints are absent or RBAC-restricted.
  * Auto-Discovered kube-state-metrics (KSM) Enrichment
    (metrics/ksm, config, cmd)
    - Streaming Allowlist Parser & Service-Proxy Discovery
      - Problem / Context: Cluster governance state—such as HPA
        scaling limits, PDB zero-disruption budgets, ResourceQuota
        saturation, CronJob schedule timestamps, pod disruption
        reasons, and DRA ResourceClaim mappings—was not surfaced in
        ktop without manually inspecting multiple API resources.
      - Technical Implementation: Added metrics/ksm
        (metrics/ksm/types.go, metrics/ksm/parser.go,
        metrics/ksm/collector.go) with a line-by-line streaming
        allowlist parser (ParseStream) that skips non-allowlisted
        series before label parsing and extracts:
        - kube_horizontalpodautoscaler_* (info, spec_min_replicas,
          spec_max_replicas, status_current_replicas,
          status_desired_replicas, status_condition)
        - kube_poddisruptionbudget_status_* (current_healthy,
          desired_healthy, expected_pods, pod_disruptions_allowed)
        - kube_resourcequota (hard, used, computed UsedPct)
        - kube_cronjob_* (spec_suspend, status_active,
          status_last_schedule_time, next_schedule_time)
        - kube_pod_status_disruption_reason and
          kube_pod_resourceclaim_info
      - Added config.NormalizeKSMMode (config/config.go),
        metrics.ksm_mode / metrics.ksm_endpoint config keys, and
        --ksm (auto default, off) / --ksm-endpoint CLI flags
        (cmd/ktop.go).
      - APIs / Signatures:

        # Default auto-discovery via API-server service proxy (degrades silently when absent)
        ktop

        # Disable KSM discovery
        ktop --ksm=off

        # Explicit service proxy or direct HTTP URL override
        ktop --ksm-endpoint=monitoring/kube-state-metrics:8080
        ktop --ksm-endpoint=http://127.0.0.1:8080/metrics

      - Behavioral Notes: Auto-discovery scans kube-system,
        monitoring, observability, prometheus, and the configured
        namespace for matching kube-state-metrics services and
        streams /metrics through the Kubernetes API server service
        proxy with zero port-forwarding. Missing or RBAC-forbidden
        services degrade silently without blocking startup.
  * Component SLIs (/metrics/slis) & Kubelet Probes
    (/metrics/probes) (metrics/sli, views/model, k8s)
    - Control-Plane & Kubelet SLI Scraping with health_score
      Integration
      - Problem / Context: API reachability alone could not detect
        internal component degradation (such as failing etcd
        readiness checks or kubelet syncloop failures) or
        containers experiencing repeated probe failures.
      - Technical Implementation: Added metrics/sli
        (metrics/sli/types.go, metrics/sli/parser.go,
        metrics/sli/collector.go) scraping GET /metrics/slis on the
        API server and nodes/{node}/proxy/metrics/slis +
        nodes/{node}/proxy/metrics/probes across nodes with bounded
        concurrency and atomic lock-free Latest() snapshots.
        Updated model.CalculateHealthScore
        (views/model/summary_model.go) and
        Controller.BuildClusterSummary (k8s/summary_controller.go).
      - Behavioral Notes:
        - When /metrics/slis is reachable and explicitly reports
          failing checks (kubernetes_healthcheck == 0),
          CalculateHealthScore deducts 15 points per unhealthy
          component (capped at 30).
        - When /metrics/slis is unavailable or RBAC-forbidden, ktop
          applies zero penalty to health_score.
        - Kubelet prober_probe_total counters aggregate
          per-container Readiness, Liveness, and Startup failure
          counts per pod.
  * Snapshot Join, Overview Layout & Detail Surfacing
    (internal/snapshot, collector, views/overview, views/workloads,
    views/pod, docs)
    - Lock-Free Snapshot & --noui Schema Extensions
      - Technical Implementation: Added optional Governance
        *GovernanceData (json:"governance,omitempty") and SLIs
        *SLIData (json:"slis,omitempty") to snapshot.Snapshot
        (internal/snapshot/snapshot.go,
        internal/snapshot/builder.go) and collector.Aggregate
        (collector/collector.go), plus pod-level disruption_reason,
        resource_claims, and failing_probes fields and SLI/KSM
        rollup counts on SummaryData. Updated
        K8sSnapshotProvider.WaitReady (collector/k8s_provider.go)
        with a bounded best-effort initial KSM/SLI scrape so
        single-shot ktop --noui captures them immediately.
    - Overview Cluster Summary & Detail Panel Surfacing
      - Problem / Context: On terminals with 45 rows or fewer,
        Overview's Cluster Summary previously hid both the top
        resource stats row and bottom enhanced stats row, leaving
        only sparklines visible.
      - Technical Implementation:
        - Updated views/overview/summary_panel.go and
          views/overview/main_panel.go to keep the full Cluster
          Summary visible below 45 rows using compact 1-row
          borderless stats lines (summaryHeight = 9 in Prometheus
          mode / 8 in non-Prometheus mode, trimming 3 rows from the
          flex Pods table).
        - Added SLIs: OK|<N> fail, Probes: <N> fail, and KSM:
          OK|<alerts> status badges to the bottom Cluster Summary
          line under the sparklines.
        - Surfaced HPA and PDB rows in Workload Detail
          (views/workloads/detail.go, k8s/workloads_controller.go),
          and failing Probes, Disrupt, and DRA Claims lines in Pod
          Detail (views/pod/detail.go,
          views/overview/main_panel.go).
        - Documented --ksm, --ksm-endpoint, governance, and slis in
          docs/cli.md and docs/noui.md.
  * Upgrade & Compatibility Notes
    - Backward Compatibility: Fully backward compatible with
      existing ktop CLI flags, kubectl ktop plugin usage,
      ~/.ktop/config.yaml configurations, and --noui JSON/JSONL
      consumers (governance, slis, and new summary/pod fields are
      additive omitempty fields).
    - Deprecations & Retractions: None.
    - Migration Actions: None required. Clusters without
      kube-state-metrics or /metrics/slis access continue operating
      with no configuration changes and zero health_score penalty.

