Mon Nov 23 06:01:42 UTC 2026 - Johannes Kastl <opensuse_buildservice@ojkastl.de>

- Update to version 0.7.5:
  ktop v0.7.5 aligns Kubernetes client and metrics support with
  Kubernetes v1.35–v1.37 (k8s.io/* v0.37.2), unifies workload state
  into the core snapshot and headless --noui JSON/JSONL schema,
  extracts shared UI-agnostic telemetry, log streaming, and YAML
  helpers, and adds full-object Node YAML inspection parity.
  Clusters running Kubernetes v1.37 now negotiate the GA
  metrics.k8s.io/v1 API with automatic v1beta1 fallback, pods using
  Pod-Level Resources (pod.Spec.Resources) or In-Place Pod Vertical
  Scaling (AllocatedResources and
  PodResizePending/PodResizeInProgress conditions) report accurate
  effective budgets and resize states in both the TUI and --noui
  output, and operators inspecting nodes in Node Detail can press v
  to open a scrollable YAML modal.
  * Kubernetes v1.35–v1.37 Client, Metrics, and Pod Resource
    Support (k8s, metrics/k8s, views/model, views/pod,
    internal/snapshot)
    - k8s.io/* v0.37.2 Upgrade & metrics.k8s.io/v1 GA Negotiation
      - Problem / Context: Previous releases pinned k8s.io/*
        dependencies to v0.35.0 and queried only
        metrics.k8s.io/v1beta1, missing the GA metrics.k8s.io/v1
        API introduced in Kubernetes v1.37 and newer client-go
        WatchList semantics.
      - Technical Implementation: Upgraded k8s.io/api,
        k8s.io/apimachinery, k8s.io/cli-runtime, k8s.io/client-go,
        and k8s.io/metrics to v0.37.2 in go.mod. Added
        Client.MetricsAPIVersion() in k8s/client.go to discover
        metrics.k8s.io/v1 and fall back to metrics.k8s.io/v1beta1.
        Updated MetricsServerSource in
        metrics/k8s/metrics_server_source.go with MetricsV1()
        queries (convertNodeMetricsV1, convertPodMetricsV1),
        automatic NotFound downgrade to MetricsV1beta1(), and
        accurate SourceInfo.Version reporting ("v1" or "v1beta1").
      - APIs / Signatures:

        apiVersion := client.MetricsAPIVersion() // "v1", "v1beta1", or ""

    - Pod-Level Resources & In-Place Pod Vertical Scaling
      - Problem / Context: Pod CPU and memory totals previously
        summed only per-container Spec.Containers[*].Resources,
        omitting pod-level budgets (pod.Spec.Resources) and
        in-place vertical resize allocations
        (ContainerStatus.AllocatedResources /
        ContainerStatus.Resources), and leaving PodResizePending /
        PodResizeInProgress conditions invisible.
      - Technical Implementation: Added GetEffectiveResources() and
        GetPodResizeStatus() in views/model/pod_model.go and
        views/model/pod_detail_data.go, updated
        GetPodContainerSummary() and GetConditions() health
        mapping, surfaced ResizeStatus
        (json:"resize_status,omitempty") on snapshot.PodData in
        internal/snapshot/snapshot.go and
        internal/snapshot/builder.go, and updated
        views/pod/detail.go to display pod-level resource headers
        ((pod-level)) and active resize status (Pending, Deferred,
        Infeasible, InProgress).
      - Behavioral Notes:
        - When pod.Spec.Resources defines a pod-level CPU or memory
          request/limit, ktop displays that effective pod budget
          instead of double-counting container specs.
        - When a container has AllocatedResources or
          Status.Resources from an in-place resize, active
          requests/limits reflect the live allocated values rather
          than stale spec values.
        - PodResizePending with reason Infeasible or Deferred
          surfaces as an unhealthy condition in Pod Detail and
          populates resize_status in --noui JSON/JSONL snapshots.
  * Unified Workloads Snapshot & Shared Runtime Helpers
    (internal/snapshot, collector, internal/history, k8s, ui,
    views/container)
    - Workloads in internal/snapshot and --noui JSON/JSONL Output
      - Problem / Context: Workload inventories (Deployments,
        StatefulSets, DaemonSets, Jobs) were previously fetched
        only inside the interactive Workloads view and were absent
        from snapshot.Snapshot and --noui JSON/JSONL outputs.
      - Technical Implementation: Added WorkloadsData,
        DeploymentData, StatefulSetData, DaemonSetData, and JobData
        to snapshot.Snapshot (json:"workloads,omitempty") with
        deep-copy support in Snapshot.Clone()
        (internal/snapshot/snapshot.go) and conversion helpers
        (ToWorkloadsSnapshot) in internal/snapshot/builder.go.
        Wired ctrl.GetWorkloadsSnapshot(ctx) in
        collector/k8s_provider.go and added Workloads
        *snapshot.WorkloadsData (json:"workloads,omitempty") to
        collector.Aggregate (collector/collector.go).
      - APIs / Signatures:

        {
          "workloads": {
            "deployments": [{ "namespace": "default", "name": "api", "desired": 3, "ready": 3, "available": 3 }],
            "statefulsets": [],
            "daemonsets": [],
            "jobs": []
          }
        }

    - Renderer-Agnostic History Store, Log Streamer, and
      Secret-Redacting YAML Formatter
      - Problem / Context: Rolling telemetry buffers, container log
        streaming cancellation, and YAML serialization with
        metadata.managedFields stripping lived inside individual
        TUI views, duplicating logic and coupling non-UI mechanics
        to tview.
      - Technical Implementation:
        - Added internal/history.Store (internal/history/store.go),
          a thread-safe bounded sample store fed by
          Store.PushSnapshot(*snapshot.Snapshot) with windowed
          slice extraction (WindowSlice) and top-N node chart
          series extraction (Extract).
        - Added k8s.LogStreamer (k8s/log_streamer.go), managing a
          single cancellable container log stream via Start / Stop
          callbacks; updated views/container/detail.go to delegate
          stream lifecycle management to k8s.LogStreamer.
        - Added k8s.FormatObjectYAML(obj any) (string, error)
          (k8s/yaml.go), which strips metadata.managedFields and
          redacts Secret.data and Secret.stringData values to
          <redacted> without mutating source objects; updated
          ui/yaml_modal.go and views/container/spec.go to delegate
          to it.
      - APIs / Signatures:

        yamlText, err := k8s.FormatObjectYAML(obj)

        store := history.NewStore(history.DefaultMaxSamples)
        store.PushSnapshot(snap)
        series := store.Extract(15*time.Minute, 5)

  * Node Detail YAML Inspection & Reliability (views/node,
    views/overview, ui, docs, tests)
    - Node YAML Modal Parity
      - Problem / Context: Workloads and Pod detail views supported
        full-object YAML inspection via v, whereas Node Detail had
        no YAML inspection action.
      - Technical Implementation: Added
        DetailPanel.SetOnShowYAML(func(*corev1.Node)) and [v] key
        handling (suppressed while filtering the pods table) in
        views/node/detail.go, wired centered ui.NewYAMLModal
        presentation with focus restoration in
        views/overview/main_panel.go, and added the [v] yaml hint
        to NodeDetailContext in ui/footer_context.go.
    - Headless E2E WatchList & Timing Hardening
      - Problem / Context: client-go v0.37.2 SharedInformer
        defaults to WatchList (sendInitialEvents=true) and expects
        an initial-events BOOKMARK before marking caches synced;
        additionally, parallel test runs could trigger watch
        transitions before initial sync completed.
      - Technical Implementation: Updated mock API server handlers
        in tests/headless_e2e_test.go to emit ADDED + BOOKMARK
        (k8s.io/initial-events-end: "true") on
        sendInitialEvents=true requests and synchronized
        watch-transition test setup on initial BOOKMARK completion.
        Updated docs/noui.md with the new workloads and pod
        resize_status schema fields.
  * Upgrade & Compatibility Notes
    - Backward Compatibility: Fully backward compatible with
      existing ktop CLI flags, kubectl ktop plugin usage,
      ~/.ktop/config.yaml configurations, and --noui JSON/JSONL
      consumers (workloads and resize_status are additive omitempty
      fields).
    - Deprecations & Retractions: None.
    - Migration Actions: None required. Builds from source require
      Go 1.27.0+ per go.mod (k8s.io/* v0.37.2).
- Update to version 0.7.4:
  ktop v0.7.4 refines the Workloads experience and introduces a
  shared floating Pod / Container / YAML Inspector modal,
  streamlining multi-page navigation and aligning table telemetry
  and colors across Overview and Workloads.
  Workloads tables now display aggregated live CPU and MEM usage
  directly across Deployments, StatefulSets, and DaemonSets,
  workload detail subpages provide richer rollout metadata with
  full-object YAML inspection, and drilling into pods or container
  logs from Overview, Node Detail, or Workload Detail opens in a
  single transparent-margin modal frame that keeps the cluster
  header, tabs, parent edges, and footer visible around it.
  * Shared Floating Pod / Container / YAML Inspector Modal (ui,
    views/overview, views/pod, views/container, application)
    - Transparent-Margin Overlay Frame & Single-Modal Leaf
      Inspection
      - Problem / Context: Opening Pod Detail, Container Logs, and
        Container Spec from Overview, Node Detail, and Workload
        Detail previously replaced the entire viewport across 4–5
        stack levels, hiding parent context and allowing circular
        Pod -> Node -> Pod navigation loops.
      - Technical Implementation: Added ui.OverlayFrame in
        ui/overlay.go to position floating modals within outer
        margins without clearing underlying cells, keeping the top
        Cluster Header, TabFrame tabs and breadcrumbs, parent page
        edges, and bottom Context Footer visible. Hosted
        views/pod.DetailPanel, views/container.DetailPanel, and
        inline YAML views inside a single modal-backed *tview.Pages
        (pod-inspector) in views/overview/main_panel.go, tracked
        separately from the underlying page state in
        views/overview/view_state.go. Updated
        Application.NavigateToPodDetail and
        Application.NavigateToContainerLogs in
        application/app_ctrl.go to delegate to the shared modal
        without pushing onto NavigationStack, capping full-screen
        drill-down depth at 1 subpage (Node Detail or <Kind>
        Detail).
      - APIs / Signatures:

        overlay := ui.NewOverlayFrame(inspectorPages, 4, 3, 3, 3)
        box, textView := ui.NewYAMLBox(ui.YAMLModalConfig{
            Title:   "Pod YAML: default/api-0",
            Content: yamlText,
            OnClose: onClose,
        })

      - Behavioral Notes:
        - Pressing Enter on any pod row in Overview, Node Detail,
          or Workload Detail opens the floating Pod Inspector modal
          (v switches inline to Pod YAML, Enter on a container
          switches inline to Container Logs, s on Container Detail
          switches inline to Container Spec YAML).
        - ESC unwinds cleanly inside the modal (YAML -> Container
          Logs -> Pod Detail -> Close Modal) and restores focus and
          footer context directly to the active parent table behind
          it (views/container/detail.go, views/node/detail.go,
          application/app_ctrl.go).
        - Added Controller.GetPod fallback in
          views/overview/main_panel.go and nil-safe metrics
          handling in model.NewPodModel (views/model/pod_model.go)
          so opening a pod from --page=workloads succeeds even
          before Overview's pod cache populates.
  * Workloads Table Telemetry, Layout & Color Alignment
    (views/workloads, views/model, k8s, ui)
    - Live Aggregated CPU & MEM Columns and Compact Single-Line
      Summary
      - Problem / Context: Workloads tables previously showed
        duplicate replica columns (UP, AVAIL, DESIRED, CURRENT)
        alongside a request-only EFF column that rendered n/a
        whenever pods omitted resources.requests, and used a
        two-row summary header duplicating the top-bar namespace
        display.
      - Technical Implementation: Added model.WorkloadUsage and
        model.ComputePodsUsage in views/model/workload_model.go
        (populated in k8s/workloads_controller.go) to sum live CPU
        and memory usage across each workload's active owned pods,
        with CPU (c) and MEM (e) sort support. Standardized
        Deployments, StatefulSets, and DaemonSets onto a unified
        7-column layout (NS | NAME | READY | CPU | MEM | AGE |
        STATUS) with ready/desired ratios in READY, and collapsed
        views/workloads/summary.go into a single-line Summary bar
        without Namespace.
      - Behavioral Notes: Aligned Workloads colors with Overview in
        views/workloads/summary.go, views/workloads/page.go, and
        ui/theme.go: Summary labels and separators use DataPrimary,
        live CPU and MEM values use DataSecondary on healthy rows,
        READY and AGE inherit rowColor, and Scaled 0 maps to
        StatusMuted so scaled-to-zero deployments recede visually
        as idle.
  * Redesigned Workload Detail Subpage & Full-Object YAML Modal
    (views/workloads, k8s, ui)
    - Kind-Specific Detail Subpages & Scrollable ui.YAMLModal
      - Problem / Context: Workload detail subpages used a generic
        Workload Detail heading, crowded replica counts into a
        single parenthetical string, devoted 4 vertical rows to
        request-ratio sparklines, and omitted key rollout fields
        (container images, revision, active ReplicaSet, strategy
        parameters, and full YAML).
      - Technical Implementation: Added ui.YAMLModal,
        ui.FormatObjectYAML (marshaling typed Kubernetes objects
        with apiVersion/kind preserved and metadata.managedFields
        stripped), and shared ui.HighlightYAML in ui/yaml_modal.go
        (reused by views/container/spec.go). Enriched
        model.WorkloadDetailData (views/model/workload_model.go,
        k8s/workloads_controller.go) and redesigned
        views/workloads/detail.go:
        - Kind-specific section headers (Deployments > <name>,
          StatefulSets > <name>, DaemonSets > <name>, Jobs >
          <name>) and detail panel titles (Deployment Detail,
          StatefulSet Detail, DaemonSet Detail, Job Detail).
        - Single-line Info bar with separate replica/job counters
          (Status, Desired, Ready, Updated, Available, Unavailable,
          PAUSED, Age).
        - Removed detail sparklines and unused aggregatePodHistory
          queries, replacing them with live used / req / lim CPU
          and memory totals, rollout strategy details, revision and
          active ReplicaSet, container images, generation lag
          highlights, and unhealthy condition messages.
        - Made <Kind> Detail active on entry (Tab cycles Detail ->
          Owned Pods -> Events) so pressing Enter opens the full
          object YAML in ui.YAMLModal (↑↓/j/k, PgUp/PgDn, g/G, y
          copy, Esc/q close). Replaced the redundant NAMESPACE
          column in Owned Pods with NODE.
  * Upgrade & Compatibility Notes
    - Backward Compatibility: Fully backward compatible with
      existing ktop CLI flags, kubectl ktop plugin usage, --noui
      JSON/JSONL output schemas, and ~/.ktop/config.yaml
      configurations.
    - Deprecations & Retractions: Removed the circular n (Pod ->
      Node) jump inside the Pod Inspector modal to keep modal
      navigation bounded.
    - Migration Actions: None required.
- Update to version 0.7.3:
  ktop v0.7.3 introduces the Workloads top-level page ([2]
  Workloads), providing real-time visibility into Deployments,
  StatefulSets, DaemonSets, and Jobs alongside a dedicated Workload
  Detail drill-down view, workload resource efficiency scoring
  (EFF), and --page=workloads startup support.
  This release also upgrades the multi-page navigation chrome with
  a bordered ui.TabFrame container that renders zero-gap themed tab
  pills and right-aligned drill-down breadcrumbs along its top
  border, refines tab color contrast across Dark, Light, ANSI, and
  Monochrome themes, and streamlines Tab focus cycling on both
  Overview and Workloads pages.
  * Workloads Informer Controller & Efficiency View Models (k8s,
    views/model)
    - Dedicated Workload Informer Snapshot & Pod Ownership
      Resolution
      - Problem / Context: ktop previously surfaced cluster state
        through Nodes and Pods without aggregating controller-level
        workload health, replica status, job completion state, or
        pod-to-workload ownership chains.
      - Technical Implementation: Added k8s/workloads_controller.go
        and views/model/workload_model.go to watch apps/v1
        (Deployment, StatefulSet, DaemonSet, ReplicaSet) and
        batch/v1 (Job) objects through Kubernetes shared informers,
        resolve owned pods via OwnerReferences (including
        Deployment -> ReplicaSet -> Pod indirection), and build
        immutable model.WorkloadsSnapshot updates. Added
        ClientController.SetWorkloadsRefreshFunc and deferred
        workload startup handling in k8s/client_controller.go so
        informer callbacks register reliably regardless of page
        initialization order. Extracted shared GetEventsForObject
        and workload object getters in k8s/client_funcs.go.
      - APIs / Signatures:

        snap, err := client.Controller().GetWorkloadsSnapshot(ctx)
        detail, err := client.Controller().GetWorkloadDetail(ctx, kind, namespace, name)

      - Behavioral Notes: Workloads snapshots honor the active
        cluster namespace filter (--namespace or header / filter),
        expose per-kind summary counts (model.WorkloadSummary), and
        compute workload health statuses (Healthy, Progressing,
        Degraded, Scaled to 0, Complete, Running, Failed).
    - Resource Request Efficiency Scoring (EFF)
      - Problem / Context: Operators inspecting controller fleets
        need a quick indicator of over-provisioned or unrequested
        CPU/memory allocations across owned pods.
      - Technical Implementation: Implemented
        model.ComputeWorkloadEfficiency in
        views/model/workload_model.go and ui.FormatEfficiencyCell
        in ui/format.go to compare live pod CPU/memory usage
        against pod requests and classify workloads into efficiency
        bands (Optimal, Underutilized, Over-provisioned, No
        Requests, No Metrics).
      - Behavioral Notes: Efficiency cells degrade gracefully when
        metrics are unavailable or pods omit resource requests, and
        use semantic theme colors (or plain text labels in
        monochrome / $NO_COLOR mode).
  * Workloads Page & Workload Detail View (views/workloads,
    application, ui)
    - 2-Column Workloads Dashboard ([2] Workloads)
      - Problem / Context: Monitoring four workload controller
        types simultaneously requires balanced screen density
        without horizontal column overflow.
      - Technical Implementation: Added views/workloads/page.go,
        views/workloads/summary.go, and views/workloads/table.go
        implementing the [2] Workloads page registered in
        application/tui/app.go. The layout pairs a compact Workload
        Summary header with an equal 2-column × 2-row tview.Grid
        (Deployments and DaemonSets on the left; StatefulSets and
        Jobs on the right), column sorting (</> or header hotkeys),
        inline filtering (/), and clipboard copy (y).
      - Behavioral Notes: NAME columns expand to use available
        width while compact metadata columns (NS, READY, UP, AVAIL,
        AGE, EFF, STATUS) stay tightly sized.
    - Workload Detail Drill-Down & Cross-View Navigation
      - Problem / Context: Investigating an unhealthy or
        inefficient Deployment, StatefulSet, DaemonSet, or Job
        requires inspecting controller metadata, live resource
        sparklines, recent Kubernetes events, and owned pods in one
        view.
      - Technical Implementation: Added views/workloads/detail.go
        and application.PageWorkloadDetail routing in
        application/navigation.go, application/page_registry.go,
        and application/app_ctrl.go. Selecting any workload row
        (Enter) opens Workload Detail with controller metadata,
        labels/annotations, live CPU/Memory/Network/Disk
        sparklines, owned pods, and workload-scoped Kubernetes
        events. Pressing Enter on an owned pod drills further into
        Pod Detail and Container Logs with full breadcrumb tracking
        (Workloads › deploy/<ns>/<name> › pod/<ns>/<pod>) and ESC
        stack unwinding.
      - Behavioral Notes: Added ui.WorkloadsContext and
        ui.WorkloadDetailContext in ui/footer_context.go, workload
        status styling in ui/theme.go, and Workloads keybindings in
        ui/help_modal.go.
  * Bordered Tab Frame, Tab Theme Contrast & Navigation Polish (ui,
    application, config)
    - Bordered ui.TabFrame Container with Top-Border Tabs and
      Breadcrumbs
       - Problem / Context: Top-level page tabs previously floated
         on a separate borderless row above the page panels,
         leaving no visual frame tying active page content to its
         selected tab.
       - Technical Implementation: Added ui.TabFrame in
         ui/tab_bar.go wrapping p.pages in application/app_ui.go
         inside a single-line bordered box (Palette.BorderNormal).
         Contiguous zero-gap tab pills render directly along the
         top border line on the left, while drill-down breadcrumbs
         render right-aligned on the same border row. Updated
         ExtraLarge panel height calculation in
         views/overview/main_panel.go for the frame borders.
       - APIs / Signatures:

         frame := ui.NewTabFrame(pages)
         frame.SetTabs([]ui.TabItem{
             {ID: "overview", Title: "Overview", Key: '1'},
             {ID: "workloads", Title: "Workloads", Key: '2'},
         })
         frame.SetActive(1)
         frame.SetBreadcrumb("Workloads › deploy/default/api")

       - Behavioral Notes: TabFrame renders its outer frame with
         single-line borders while inner tables retain focus
         borders, and delegates Focus, Blur, HasFocus,
         InputHandler, and MouseHandler directly to the active
         page.
    - Dedicated Active/Inactive Tab Palette Tokens & Streamlined
      Tab Cycling
      - Technical Implementation: Added TabActiveFg, TabActiveBg,
        TabInactiveFg, and TabInactiveBg tokens to
        ui/theme/palette.go and tuned Dark, Light, ANSI, and
        Monochrome presets in ui/theme/builtins.go for clear
        active/inactive separation and readability. Removed
        non-interactive Summary boxes (Cluster Summary and Workload
        Summary) from the Tab focus cycle in
        views/overview/main_panel.go, views/workloads/page.go, and
        application/tui/app.go so Tab cycles directly across
        interactive panels (Header -> Nodes -> Pods on Overview;
        Header -> Deployments -> StatefulSets -> DaemonSets -> Jobs
        on Workloads).
    - Startup Page Configuration (--page=workloads) & Diverse Load
      Test Harness
      - Technical Implementation: Added workloads to
        config.ValidPages (config/config.go) and updated CLI flag
        help (cmd/ktop.go), allowing startup directly on Workloads
        via ktop --page=workloads or ui.default_page: workloads in
        ~/.ktop/config.yaml. Expanded
        hack/load-test/deploy-load.sh,
        hack/load-test/cleanup-load.sh, and
        hack/load-test/README.md to provision diverse Deployments
        (including over-provisioned and scaled-to-zero examples),
        StatefulSets, DaemonSets, Jobs, and CronJobs for local
        verification.
  * Upgrade & Compatibility Notes
    - Backward Compatibility: Fully backward compatible with
      existing ktop CLI invocations, kubectl ktop plugin usage,
      --noui JSON/JSONL output schemas, and ~/.ktop/config.yaml
      configurations. Existing installations without
      ui.default_page continue opening on overview.
    - Deprecations & Retractions: None.
    - Migration Actions: None required.

