Wed Nov 18 05:56:48 UTC 2026 - Johannes Kastl <opensuse_buildservice@ojkastl.de>

- Update to version 0.7.2:
  ktop v0.7.2 introduces the multi-page terminal UI navigation
  architecture, adding a theme-aware top-level tab bar (ui.TabBar)
  with drill-down breadcrumbs, a declarative page registry
  (application.PageDescriptor and application.PageSession),
  isolated per-page navigation stacks
  (application.NavigationStack), keyboard page-switching shortcuts
  (1–9, [ and ]), and startup page configuration via --page and
  ui.default_page in ~/.ktop/config.yaml.
  Top-level pages maintain independent focus positions and
  drill-down histories across tab transitions while sharing cluster
  header namespace filtering, modal overlays, and Kubernetes
  informer lifecycles.
  * Top-Level Tab Bar & Breadcrumb Navigation (ui)
    - Theme-Aware Tab Bar and Right-Aligned Drill-Down Breadcrumbs
      - Problem / Context: ktop previously rendered a single
        unindexed page container without visible top-level tab
        indicators or hierarchical location trails when navigating
        across nested Node, Pod, and Container detail views.
      - Implementation Details: Added ui.TabBar and ui.TabItem in
        ui/tab_bar.go backed by a 1-row borderless tview.Table
        mounted directly beneath the cluster header in
        application/app_ui.go (removing the unmounted legacy
        page-button footer table and updating panel height
        calculations in views/overview/main_panel.go). Added
        application.FormatBreadcrumb in application/navigation.go
        to render active drill-down paths (<Page> › node/<name> ›
        pod/<ns>/<pod> › logs/<container>).
      - APIs / Signatures:

        tb := ui.NewTabBar()
        tb.SetTabs([]ui.TabItem{
            {ID: "overview", Title: "Overview", Key: '1'},
        })
        tb.SetActive(0)
        tb.SetBreadcrumb("Overview › node/worker-1 › pod/default/api-0")

      - Impact & Behavioral Notes: Active tabs render with
        Palette.HeaderFg on Palette.HeaderBg (and tcell.AttrReverse
        | tcell.AttrBold with tcell.ColorDefault in monochrome and
        $NO_COLOR environments); inactive tabs and breadcrumbs
        render with Palette.CanvasFg on Palette.CanvasBg.
        Root-level pages omit redundant breadcrumb text and display
        trail segments only when drilled into detail views. Updated
        ui.OverviewContext, ui.PageContext (ui/footer_context.go),
        and ui.HelpModal (ui/help_modal.go) to display dynamic
        [1-N] page and [ / ] shortcuts.
  * Multi-Page Registry, Per-Page Navigation Stacks & Input Routing
    (application, k8s, views)
    - Declarative Page Registry and Isolated Per-Page Sessions
      - Problem / Context: Focus management, Tab/Shift+Tab panel
        cycling, ESC back-navigation, modal focus restoration, and
        active detail lookups in application/app_ctrl.go previously
        indexed app.pages[0] directly and shared a single
        NavigationStack rooted at PageOverview.
      - Implementation Details: Added application.PageDescriptor
        and application.PageSession in application/page_registry.go
        (RegisterPage, PageCount, ActivePageIndex, ActivePageID,
        FindPageIndex, SetInitialPage, SwitchToPageIndex,
        SwitchToPage, NextPage, PrevPage) and
        application.NewNavigationStackWithRoot in
        application/navigation.go. Refactored
        application/app_ctrl.go to resolve focus, EscapablePanel
        state, HelpModal context, and ESC unwind transitions
        against the active PageSession, added
        Application.SetDetailResetCallback and
        Application.AddNamespaceFilterListener, added
        DetailPanel.IsFilterEditing in views/container/detail.go,
        and guarded Controller.Start in k8s/client_controller.go
        for idempotent informer startup across multiple registered
        pages.
      - APIs / Signatures:

        app.RegisterPage(application.PageDescriptor{
            ID:         "overview",
            Title:      "Overview",
            Key:        '1',
            RootType:   application.PageOverview,
            Panel:      overviewPage,
            ChildNames: []string{"summary", "nodes", "pods"},
        })

      - Impact & Behavioral Notes: Pressing 1–9 switches directly
        to the corresponding registered page, and [ / ] cycles to
        the previous or next page with wrap-around. Switching away
        from a page preserves both its focused panel index and any
        open detail stack (Node Detail, Pod Detail, Container
        Logs), restoring them when switching back. When any filter
        input is active (cluster header namespace filter, table /
        filter, or container log filter), digit and bracket keys
        pass directly into the text input without triggering page
        switches.
  * CLI & Configuration (cmd, config, application/tui)
    - Startup Page Flag (--page) and Persistent Default
      (ui.default_page)
      - Problem / Context: Operators had no CLI flag or
        configuration key to select or validate the initial
        top-level page at startup.
      - Implementation Details: Added --page in cmd/ktop.go,
        InitialPage on tui.Options in application/tui/app.go, and
        UIConfig.DefaultPage (ui.default_page), config.ValidPages,
        and config.NormalizePage in config/config.go.
      - APIs / Signatures:

        # Launch ktop on a specific top-level page
        ktop --page=overview

        # ~/.ktop/config.yaml
        ui:
          theme: auto
          color_mode: auto
          default_page: overview

      - Impact & Behavioral Notes: --page defaults to overview and
        overrides ui.default_page in ~/.ktop/config.yaml for the
        current session. Unrecognized --page or ui.default_page
        values fail fast prior to cluster connection with exit code
        2 (ExitInvalidFlags).
  * Upgrade & Compatibility Notes
    - Backward Compatibility: Fully backward compatible with
      existing ktop CLI invocations, kubectl ktop plugin usage,
      --noui JSON/JSONL schemas, and ~/.ktop/config.yaml files.
      Existing configurations without ui.default_page default
      automatically to overview.
    - Deprecations & Retractions: None.
    - Migration Actions: None required.


