- Update to version 0.6.1:
  ktop v0.6.1 delivers UI ergonomics, subpage polish, and expanded
  multi-OS distribution. This release adds interactive column
  sorting and filtering to the Pod Detail Containers table,
  surfaces live Pressure Stall Information (PSI) metrics directly
  within Node and Pod detail headers, introduces an interactive
  keyboard shortcut overlay modal (? or F1), enables direct
  clipboard copying for selected resource names (y), adds CLI flags
  for initial table sorting (--sort-nodes, --sort-pods), and
  packages native Windows binary builds and zip archives in
  automated releases.
  * Pod Detail Containers Table Sorting & Filtering (#165)
    - Interactive Sorting: Added interactive column sorting to the
      Containers table in the Pod Detail page with hotkey bindings:
      c (CPU), m (Memory), n (Name), i (Image), s (Status), and r
      (Restarts).
    - Persistent Direction: Preserves active sort column and
      direction across periodic metric refresh cycles.
    - Filter Support: Integrated slash (/) filtering to quickly
      search and filter container names within pods.
  * Detail Views PSI Resource Stall Indicators (#168)
    - Info Header PSI Metrics: Integrated live Pressure Stall
      Information (PSI) metrics (CPU, MEM, IO) directly into the
      condensed Info header box on both Node Detail and Pod Detail
      pages.
    - Color Thresholds: Displays stall percentages styled by
      severity: green (<2%), yellow (2–10%), orange (10–25%), and
      red (≥25%).
    - Kernel Guardrail: Renders PSI: ⚠ N/A when running against
      nodes with Linux kernels older than 4.20 where PSI is
      unsupported.
    - Vertical Space Conservation: Retains a single compact
      sparkline row (CPU, MEM, Net, Disk), preserving terminal
      space for the Containers and Pods tables.
  * Keyboard Shortcut Help Overlay Modal (#169)
    - Contextual Help Modal: Added an interactive keyboard shortcut
      overlay modal triggered via ? or F1 from any page.
    - Categorized Reference: Groups all available keybindings into
      categorized sections: General Navigation, Table Controls,
      Column Customization, Detail Views, and Log Viewer.
    - Isolated Event Handling: Modal cleanly dismisses on Esc,
      Enter, or q, restoring the previous page state and table
      focus without triggering application exit.
  * Clipboard Copy for Selected Resource Names (#171)
    - Resource Yank Key: Added y shortcut key to copy the currently
      selected node, pod, or container name to the system
      clipboard.
    - Visual Feedback: Displays temporary confirmation in the
      footer upon successful copy.
  * Initial Table Sorting CLI Arguments (#174)
    - CLI Startup Flags: Introduced --sort-nodes and --sort-pods
      CLI flags to specify initial sort columns on startup (e.g.,
      ktop --sort-nodes=cpu --sort-pods=memory).
    - Input Validation: Validates user-specified sort keys against
      recognized column identifiers with helpful error diagnostics
      on invalid arguments.
  * Native Windows Binary Builds & Zip Archives (#166)
    - Windows Cross-Compilation: Configured GoReleaser to produce
      native Windows binaries (windows/amd64, windows/arm64) for
      both standalone ktop.exe and kubectl-ktop.exe plugin
      executables.
    - Zip Packaging: Configured .zip archive formats for Windows
      distribution alongside existing .tar.gz archives for Linux
      and macOS.
  * Documentation & Configuration Reference (#173)
    - Guide Updates: Updated README.md, docs/guide.md, docs/cli.md,
      and docs/psi.md documenting new CLI flags, keyboard
      shortcuts, PSI stall indicators, and multi-OS installation
      workflows.

