- Update to version 0.6.0:
  ktop v0.6.0 introduces Kubernetes Pressure Stall Information
  (PSI) resource contention metrics, a dedicated user session
  directory with rotated logging (~/.ktop/), dynamic in-app table
  column selection and configuration persistence
  (~/.ktop/config.yaml), interactive column sorting and filtering
  across subpages, major Prometheus scraper and metric store
  performance optimizations, codebase modernization, and toolchain
  upgrade to Go 1.27.
  * PSI (Pressure Stall Information) Metrics
    - Resource Contention Signals: Integrated cAdvisor/kubelet PSI
      metrics (container_pressure_cpu_waiting_seconds_total,
      container_pressure_memory_waiting_seconds_total,
      container_pressure_io_waiting_seconds_total) across node and
      pod workloads.
    - Overview STALL Column: Added a STALL column to Nodes and Pods
      overview tables rendering the dominant waiting stall
      percentage (CPU, Memory, or I/O) over the scrape window.
    - Cluster Summary Stall Gauge: Added cluster-level PSI stall
      metrics to the Cluster Summary header.
    - Version Guardrails: Added runtime version checks that surface
      ⚠ PSI beta in the cluster header when Kubernetes is <1.36 and
      prefix STALL values with ⚠ 0% when node kernels are <4.20.
  * User Session Directory & Rotated Logging (~/.ktop/)
    - Session Directory: Introduced automatic creation of ~/.ktop/
      (mode 0700) for user-specific data, relocatable via the
      $KTOP_DIR environment variable.
    - Rotated Structured Logging: Integrated log/slog and
      lumberjack.v2 writing to ~/.ktop/ktop.log (mode 0600) with
      automatic 10MB rotation, retaining the last 3 sessions
      without interfering with the terminal display.
    - CLI Logging Flags: Added --log-level (debug, info, warn,
      error) and --log-format (text, json) flags.
    - Graceful Degradation: Application continues running cleanly
      if directory or file creation fails due to restrictive
      filesystem permissions.
  * Dynamic Column Configuration & Persistence
    (~/.ktop/config.yaml)
    - Interactive Column Selector Modal: Added interactive column
      selection dialog triggered via the = hotkey on focused
      overview tables, supporting Space toggle, Enter apply, and
      Esc cancel.
    - Active Default Columns: Enforced compact default column
      layouts for Nodes (NAME, STATUS, RST, PODS, DISK, CPU, MEM)
      and Pods (NAMESPACE, POD, READY, STATUS, RST, AGE, CPU,
      MEMORY), preventing horizontal table sprawling on standard
      terminals unless explicitly requested with
      --show-all-columns.
    - Configuration Schema: Introduced ~/.ktop/config.yaml
      supporting table column customizations with resolved defaults
      for metrics collection and logging.
    - Automatic Persistence: Column selections passed via CLI flags
      (--node-columns, --pod-columns) or modified via the
      interactive modal automatically persist to
      ~/.ktop/config.yaml.
    - Modal Event Isolation: Isolated modal input capture so
      dismissing the column dialog with Esc restores table focus
      without triggering application-level exit.
  * Subpage Navigation, Sorting & UI Consolidation
    - Shared Table Controller: Extracted reusable
      ui.TableController encapsulating sort toggling, shortcut key
      binding, slash / filter lifecycle, and scroll titles.
    - Node Detail Pods Sorting & Filtering: Enabled interactive
      column sorting (c CPU, m MEM, n NAMESPACE, p POD, s STATUS, r
      RESTARTS, d READY, a AGE) and / slash filtering on the Node
      Detail Pods table.
    - Header Shortcut Collision Fix: Renamed Node Detail Pods
      second column from NAME to POD, matching the Overview page
      and fixing the hotkey collision on 'N' with NAMESPACE.
    - Format Consolidation: Unified detail formatting utilities
      (FormatCPU, FormatMemory, FormatDuration, FormatEventAge,
      Truncate, AdaptiveRateMax, CycleFocus) into ui/format.go.
  * Performance & Scraper Optimizations
    - Scraper Loop Deduplication: Eliminated duplicate background
      scrape goroutines in KubernetesScraper, halving proxy scrape
      traffic to node kubelets and cAdvisor endpoints.
    - O(S) Pod Metrics Aggregation: Rewrote GetAllPodMetrics from
      an O ( N ns × N pods × N series ) Cartesian scan into a
      single-pass O ( S ) aggregation grouped by (namespace, pod,
      container).
    - Node Metric Query Deduplication: Reused existing node metrics
      during overview and summary refresh cycles to avoid duplicate
      queries.
    - Pod-to-Node Indexing: Pre-indexed pods by Spec.NodeName in O
      ( P ) when constructing node models.
    - Sparkline Memory Leak Fix: Added automatic eviction of
      deleted pods and nodes from memory sparkline maps.
    - InitContainer Metric Correctness: Corrected CPU request
      accounting in GetPodContainerSummary for pods configured with
      init containers.
    - Informer Resilience & RBAC Fallback: Replaced background
      informer sync panics with graceful error recovery, supporting
      namespace-scoped RBAC clusters.
    - TUI Concurrency Deadlock Fix: Switched refresh queue delivery
      to non-blocking sends and debounced filter inputs to
      eliminate UI freezes.
  * Codebase Simplification & Toolchain Modernization
    - Dead Code Removal: Removed unused views/pod/logs.go and
      deprecated metrics informer/lister infrastructure in k8s/.
    - Direct Metric Summation: Eliminated redundant
      v1beta1.PodMetrics round-trip conversion in
      MainPanel.refreshPods.
    - Go 1.27 Toolchain: Upgraded module toolchain to Go 1.27
      across go.mod, Dockerfile, and GitHub Actions workflows.
    - Standard Library Idioms: Modernized codebase to use
      slices.Sort, slices.Contains, slices.Clone, and standardized
      error wrapping with %w.
    - Multi-OS CI Matrix: Expanded GitHub Actions CI test suite to
      validate builds and tests across Linux, macOS, and Windows
      (windows-latest).

